Game of Life of benchmarks/life, the demo's reference in Mercury, on small
grids, so that it keeps building and giving the right cells: sequentially,
and on the host's threads, where OpenMP runs its target regions when there
is no device, each at -O0 and -O2. The populations and checksums are from
an independent program in Python; Life is exact, so every build gives them.

RUN: merkc -O0 -fdo-loops %S/../../benchmarks/life/life.m -o %t.sequential0
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=64 LIFE_STEPS=10 %t.sequential0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %t.sequential0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LARGER
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops %S/../../benchmarks/life/life.m -o %t.sequential2
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=64 LIFE_STEPS=10 %t.sequential2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
RUN: env LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %t.sequential2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LARGER
RUN: merkc -O0 -fopenmp -fdo-loops %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life.m -o %t.host0
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %t.host0 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LARGER
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life.m -o %t.host2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_SIZE=64 LIFE_STEPS=10 %t.host2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SMALL
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %t.host2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LARGER
REQUIRES: libomp

SMALL: Game of Life, Mercury
SMALL-NEXT: Grid: 64 x 64 cells, 8 bytes a cell
SMALL-NEXT: Steps: 10
SMALL-NEXT: Population: 847
SMALL-NEXT: Checksum: 1721245
SMALL-NEXT: Gcells/sec    Min (sec)   Max         Average

LARGER: Population: 9339
LARGER-NEXT: Checksum: 429141631
